================================================================================
Complex rule builder: clickable answers for discrete-choice questions
================================================================================

Context:
When the Complex rule assistant asks a question with a small, well-defined set
of answers (a yes/no confirmation like "Does 'Active' sound like the right
value to match?", a choice between a few named values, an operator, a short
list of properties), it can now offer those answers as clickable controls in
the chat so the user clicks instead of typing. The agent is instructed to use
this ONLY for genuinely discrete questions, never for open-ended ones.
Single-select renders as pills that send on click; multi-select renders as
checkboxes + a Send button. Free-text input stays usable and answered groups
lock.

Changes:
1. src/agents/tools/context.py — new ToolContext field rule_options
   ({question, options: [str], multi}).
2. src/agents/agent_complex_rule_builder/tools.py — new propose_options tool
   (strips empty labels, stores the group or None), schema, and registration.
3. src/agents/agent_complex_rule_builder/engine.py — AgentResult.options;
   _surface_state() helper copies draft/ready/options onto the result (keeps
   run_agent under its LOC budget); SYSTEM_PROMPT step 2 + TOOLS list instruct
   the agent to call propose_options only for discrete-choice questions.
4. src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py — complex_rule_assistant_chat returns
   options in the JSON response.
5. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-business-rules.js — _craApplyResponse
   renders options via new _craRenderOptions / _craChooseOption /
   _craLockPendingOptions (pills vs checkboxes+Send, lock on answer, single live
   group); craSend/_craKickoff manage the pending group.
6. src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-business-rules.css — .cra-options /
   .cra-opt-pill / .cra-opt-check / .cra-opt-send + locked/is-chosen states.
7. tests/units/agents/test_agent_complex_rule_builder.py — tool + engine
   surfacing tests (single/multi/none).
8. tests/units/api/test_complex_rule_assistant_chat.py — options passthrough.
9. tests/units/front/test_business_rules_list_ui.py — JS/CSS contract for the
